      "text": "The failed checks exposed three concrete implementation defects, not uncertainty in the source contract: Windows text streams converted required LF bytes to CRLF, the embedded AES S-box omitted one byte, and ZipCrypto used Python’s high-level CRC convention instead of the ZIP key-schedule recurrence. I’m correcting those primitives and making all observable writes binary/LF-stable; then I’ll rerun the same failed tests unchanged, which is the necessary evidence that the fixes address causes rather than weakening assertions."
